# 1. First: What is your project actually?

Your project is:

> **An AI-powered workforce planning system that learns from historical project/workload data, predicts future workload, checks whether the available employees can handle it, identifies overload/capacity gaps, and recommends how work should be planned or redistributed.**

Think of a company manager.

Suppose the company has:

- 300 employees
- 50 projects
- 2,000 tasks
- employees with different skills
- different working hours
- different availability
- tasks with different deadlines
- historical records of how long similar tasks took
- projects starting/ending at different times

The manager wants to know:

> **“I have these projects coming up. Do I have enough people? Who is overloaded? Who has capacity? Which employee should handle which task? What will my workload look like next month?”**

Your system answers those questions.

